# Decision Records

Use stable `DEC-0001`-style identifiers. A decision is authoritative only
within its scope when its status is `accepted` and its authority source is
valid.

Do not pre-accept the generated template. Accepted records preserve their
meaning; correct them with a dated addendum or successor record.

`governance-register.json` is the project-owned inventory for material
decision questions, recommendations, owner selections, trade-off reviews,
compatibility findings, and the minimum closure sequence. Its stable
`DREG-####` IDs are tracking identities, not durable decision authority.

Use `.agent/templates/architecture-decision-register.md` for owner-friendly
review, `.agent/templates/trade-off-review.md` for evidence-based comparison,
and `.agent/templates/read-only-review.md` for review assurance. Reconcile the
machine register after a review. A recommendation is not an owner selection;
an owner selection remains pending until an accepted `DEC-####` authority
record is linked.

`reuse-policy.json` is a separate empty project-owned applicability registry.
It may project a value from an exact current accepted `DEC-####` into matching
future setup questions only while the decision bytes, authority source,
applicability, governing instructions, dependency fingerprints, and freshness
remain current. A superseded, revoked, expired, mismatched, or unresolved
decision is not reused. The registry never stores runtime authorization,
operation confirmation, external-action permission, or readiness evidence.
